# Qualcomm Wi-Fi cards ath12k drives, the family each belongs to, and the linux-firmware
# records that hold each family's board data.
#
#   record <family> <board name>        a board-2.bin entry with the family's data; the first
#                                        one the installed linux-firmware has is used
#   card <chip> <subsystem> <family>     a card, by its PCI vendor:device and subsystem IDs
#
# A family is the board file Qualcomm's Windows driver sets for the card (its INF's
# BDFileName). Every card linux-firmware lists in a family below has the same record, so a
# card it doesn't list yet gets that record. Cards are taken from qcwlanhmt8380 and
# qcwlancol8380 1.0.4516.4000 (X1), qcwlanhmt8480 00685.13804.00060 and qcwlancol8480
# 00685.13804.00110 (X2), records from linux-firmware's board-2.bin as of 781bd88c (QCC2072)
# and 575bbe3f (WCN7850). Left out: cards on the driver's default bdwlan.elf (Qualcomm's own
# 17cb:1110 and 00ab:1414), and 103c:8e64, whose family linux-firmware has no record for.

# wcn785x_2p0_ncm825: Windows sets bdwlan_wcn785x_2p0_ncm825.elf for these cards.
